{:id "0013-e2e-smoke"
 :title "End-to-end smoke: a browser talks to the agent through the emulators"
 :lupa/deps #{"0011-app-shell" "0010-dev-seed" "0005-worker" "0014-shell-timestamps"}
 ;; Respec 2026-10-21 after the first run halted at review (REWORK x2):
 ;; the smoke test was right, the shell could not decode Timestamps; fixed
 ;; by 0014. The reviewer's smaller asks are now acceptance criteria.
 :lupa/area :dev
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "`bb e2e` proves the whole loop in a real browser: emulators up and
        seeded, the worker answering with the :mock engine, the app served
        locally; a headless Chromium signs in, sends a message, and sees the
        agent's reply arrive and settle, with and without reduced motion,
        and saves screenshots."
 :scope ["package.json" "package-lock.json" "bb.edn" "e2e/smoke.mjs"
         "src/halfahead/dev/e2e.clj" "src/halfahead/dev/serve.clj"
         "test/halfahead/dev/serve_test.clj" ".gitignore"]
 :design "package.json: add devDependency \"playwright\": \"1.56.1\" (its
          Chromium revision is the one preinstalled under
          PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH; never run `playwright install`).
          Regenerate package-lock.json with npm install.

          halfahead.dev.serve (Babashka, using the bundled
          org.httpkit.server): (handler root) serves files under root with
          content types for .html .js .css .png .svg .json .map; a request
          path that resolves outside root (.. segments, encoded or not) is a
          404. (start! {:root :port}) -> a stop function.

          halfahead.dev.e2e (Babashka):
            (-main) runs `npx firebase emulators:exec --only firestore,auth
            --project demo-halfahead \"bb e2e:inner\"` (the ports in
            firebase.json; e2e runs alone).
            (inner!) compiles the app (npx shadow-cljs compile app), runs the
            seed, starts the worker (`bb worker --agent scout --engine mock`)
            as a child process, starts the static server on a free port,
            runs `node e2e/smoke.mjs <url>`, then stops the server and kills
            the worker by its own process handle (never by name), and exits
            with the smoke test's exit code. Child output goes to
            out/e2e/*.log.
          bb.edn: tasks `e2e` (-main) and `e2e:inner` (inner!).
          .gitignore: out/ is already ignored; keep it so.

          e2e/smoke.mjs (Playwright, chromium.launch()):
            1. open the URL; wait for the conversation header; assert the
               agent chip reads \"agent of Ben\".
            2. type \"Hello from the smoke test\" in the composer and press
               Enter; assert it appears as Ben's message.
            3. within 20 s, a Scout message whose .sr-only text is \"Noted:
               Hello from the smoke test\" appears; wait until every .seg in
               it has --p 1; screenshot out/e2e/conversation.png.
            4. a second browser context with reducedMotion 'reduce': send
               \"Second, without motion\"; when Scout's reply first appears,
               every .seg in it already has --p 1; screenshot
               out/e2e/reduced-motion.png.
            Print one line per step; exit non-zero with the step name and
            the page's console errors on any failure.

          If the smoke test exposes a defect in the app shell, core, views,
          or worker, do NOT fix it here: stop, and make your final message
          the failing step, the evidence (console errors, screenshot path),
          and the fix you would make. That message is the respec."
 :acceptance
 ["serve: a test starts the server on a free port over a temp dir and gets
   200 with text/html for index.html, 404 for a missing file, and 404 for
   /../bb.edn and /%2e%2e/bb.edn"
  "`bb e2e` passes in this container and leaves out/e2e/conversation.png
   and out/e2e/reduced-motion.png"
  "After `bb e2e`, no worker, server, or emulator process it started is
   still running (assert in the script or show `ps` in the final message)"
  "Cleanup runs in a finally: the worker, the static server and the
   emulators are stopped once each whether the smoke test passes or fails,
   and the final message shows `ps` output with none of them left"
  "On a failure, the screenshot is taken from the page whose step failed
   (out/e2e/failure.png), not always the first page"
  "package-lock.json changes only by adding playwright and its
   dependencies: do not let npm drop or rewrite unrelated entries
   (use `npm install --save-dev --save-exact playwright@1.56.1` against the
   committed lock and check the diff)"
  "`bb test` stays green (e2e is not part of the gate)"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit anything under src/halfahead except the two new dev
   namespaces; no app fixes"
  "Not in `bb test`; no CI workflow yet; no real engine"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/app.cljs" "src/halfahead/fx/firebase.cljs"
           "src/halfahead/config.cljc" "src/halfahead/dev/seed.clj"
           "src/halfahead/worker/main.clj" "src/halfahead/dev/emulator.clj"
           "firebase.json" "bb.edn" "package.json" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
